Don't start the jobserver by default on Cygwin.

b starts a FIFO jobserver unless told otherwise, and the monitor thread then
calls ioctl(FIONREAD) on it. On Cygwin that fails with ENOTTY, which aborts b
with std::ios_base::failure ("Inappropriate ioctl for device") as soon as it
runs with more than one job. Default to no jobserver on Cygwin; an explicit
--jobserver fifo still asks for one.

--- a/build2/b/b.cxx
+++ b/build2/b/b.cxx
@@ -506,7 +506,10 @@
       }
       else
       {
-#ifndef _WIN32
+        // The jobserver monitor needs ioctl(FIONREAD) on the FIFO, which
+        // fails with ENOTTY on Cygwin, so don't start one by default there.
+        //
+#if !defined(_WIN32) && !defined(__CYGWIN__)
         type = "fifo";
 #else
         type = nullptr;
